# Build packages in parallel, merged over a board's defconfig by
# `./builder setup <board> --parallel`.
#
# Per-package directories give every package its own copy of exactly its
# declared dependencies, which is what makes a top-level `make -jN` safe:
# `./builder build` runs one when the configuration carries this option.
# Buildroot marks it experimental. A package depending on something it never
# declared fails here rather than building by luck, so the switch is off by
# default. The include paths move into output/per-package/, so the first build
# after switching misses the compiler cache.
BR2_PER_PACKAGE_DIRECTORIES=y
